: " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Explaining How Things Were Done"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "  You use <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">was going</span> to to explain how things were done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to </span>when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. You can use this structure using the Past tense to talk about things that you were obligated to do, but didn't or couldn't do. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is: <br /><br /> Subject + To be +<span class=\"italic\"> supposed to</span> + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">was supposed to have</span> it renovated, but he never got around to doing it.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br /><br /> Like this: Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure<span class=\"strong\"> was going to </span> when you want to talk about things that you had planned or intended to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> + verb <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was going to call</span> but I haven't been down there in a while.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He was supposed to send me a contact number for someone to look 